RECOVERED, not regenerated. Provenance, in full, because these rows were typed back
rather than produced by a run:

  Source        a --longest sweep started 2026-09-03T10:43:18-0400, killed after
                3h24m having decided 3 of 2315 answers. Its rows were flushed to
                this path as they landed, exactly as intended -- and then the file
                was deleted during a "clear everything so I can restart" cleanup,
                which was asked for and disclosed but discarded the only copy of a
                3.5-hour result. Nothing had committed it, so git held no history.
  Restored from that run's captured stdout, kept verbatim beside this file as
                stall.longest.recovered.log (in data/shared/, so it TRAVELS -- the
                original log was under data/local/, which is gitignored). Every field here appears
                in that log; nothing was inferred.

WHAT IS SOUND. The VALUES: bully = 16 exactly (it was tested at 17 and failed);
burly and furry cannot beat 16 (both tested against a floor of 17 and failed).
bully's 16-guess line was separately verified against the audited model -- every
guess legal in sequence, exactly one legal word remaining at the end, and 11 of the
16 plays guess-only words rather than possible answers.

WHAT IS STALE. The `secs` column. These come from the pre-compaction binary; the
same searches now run about 3x faster. Node counts are unaffected -- the compaction
was verified to leave them bit-identical -- so `nodes` still stands.

A resumed sweep will SKIP these three answers and recover the incumbent 16 from the
bully row, which is correct: can_reach is monotone in its target, so an answer that
failed against a floor of 17 stays retired against any higher one.
